---
title: In & out
description: The layer system — twenty ways in, sixteen ways out, timed on the frame’s clock with a stagger. A layer has an in, a time and an out; it never needs two tags.
eyebrow: Content creation · Elements
source: src/studio/motion.css
---
<p>Any element in a frame is a layer. <code>data-in</code> and <code>data-out</code> name its two animations; the two times say when each starts; a parent with <code>im-studio-stagger</code> numbers its children so they arrive one after another. Both animations are declared on the one element — the in with <code>both</code> fill, the out with <code>forwards</code> — so a layer with no <code>data-out</code> simply stays.</p>
{{{{code "html"}}}}
<div class="im-studio-stagger">
	<h1 class="im-studio-title im-studio-layer" data-in="line-up" data-out="sink"
	    style="--im-studio-in-at: .4s; --im-studio-out-at: 4s">…</h1>
	<p class="im-studio-sub im-studio-layer" data-in="rise" data-out="sink"
	   style="--im-studio-in-at: .4s; --im-studio-out-at: 4s">…</p>   <!-- 90ms later, by the stagger -->
</div>
{{{{/code}}}}

