<h2>Knobs</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Default</th><th></th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>--im-studio-in-at</code> / <code>-out-at</code></td><td>0s / never</td><td>When, on the frame’s clock.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--im-studio-in-for</code> / <code>-out-for</code></td><td>slow / base</td><td>How long. The motion tokens.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--im-studio-in-ease</code> / <code>-out-ease</code></td><td>out / in</td><td>The curve. A pop sets spring, a wipe sets in-out, by itself.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--im-studio-step</code></td><td>90ms</td><td>The stagger between numbered children.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--im-studio-steps</code></td><td>24</td><td>How many characters a <code>type</code> in has.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>The ins that move text letter by letter (<code>letters</code>, <code>words</code>) need <code>data-im-split</code> on the element and <code>im-motion.js</code> on the page, which every frame loads. On the page, the same ideas are the <a href="/motion/entrances/">25 entrances</a>; these are their cousins on a clock.</p>
